where \(N\) is the number of hits for a track in the TPC, \(\left.\frac{dE}{dx}\right|_{meas.}\) is the measured energy loss of a track and \(\langle\frac{dE}{dx}\rangle_{\pi}\) is the mean energy loss for \(\pi^{\pm}\) described by the Bethe-Bloch formula [59]

\[\begin{split}\frac{dE}{dx}&=Kz^{2}\frac{Z}{A} \frac{1}{\beta^{2}}[\frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{2m_{e}c^{2}\beta^{2}\gamma^{2}T_{max} }{I^{2}}-\beta^{2}-\frac{\delta(\beta\gamma)}{2}]\\ K&=4\pi N_{A}r_{e}^{2}m_{e}c^{2},\end{split} \tag{2.2}\]

