acceptances are almost identical in embedding and real data, so the correction is negligible.

#### Efficiency

With the necessary corrections done, the total \(\pi^{0}\) detection efficiency is shown in Figure 3.24. The geometry correction is included in the figures, but the BEMC correction is applied separately to the spectra. The use of TPC photons helps improve the \(\pi^{0}\) signal resolution, but is more statistically challenging, due to the low conversion probability. Using one TPC photon instead of an EMC photon results in about a factor of 5 decrease of \(\pi^{0}\) detection efficiency. Using EMC photons enhances the efficiency significantly and is more preferable in studying \(\pi^{0}\) spectrum at high \(p_{T}\).

